# Circle entity-secret recovery files (never commit — back up offline).
# The SDK writes `recovery-file.json` by default; older flows produced .dat.
# Losing the entity secret WITHOUT this file is unrecoverable — every agent
# wallet is gone. Keep it in a password manager / secrets vault, not here.
circle-entity-secret-recovery.dat
**/circle-entity-secret-recovery.dat
recovery_file.dat
**/recovery_file.dat
recovery_file_*.dat
**/recovery_file_*.dat
recovery-file.json
**/recovery-file.json
*-recovery-file.json
**/*-recovery-file.json
*.pem

# Build output
dist/
build/
.next/
out/
.vite/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Test / coverage
coverage/
.nyc_output/
*.lcov

# Foundry
contracts/out/
contracts/cache/
contracts/broadcast/
contracts/.gas-snapshot
contracts/lib/

# Design source dropped in by `Mantua Prototype.html` for in-browser
# comparison via `client/public/_proto/`. The bundle lives in
# `~/Downloads/mantua-ai/` per the user-memory design-source rule;
# `_proto/` is just a Vite-served mirror.
client/public/_proto/

# Drizzle
drizzle/migrations/meta/_journal.json.bak

# Logs
logs/
*.log
# Slither outputs default to untracked (ad-hoc runs land here), but any
# output a security document CITES must be tracked — an audit found this
# directory empty while findings.md pointed at it. Negate per cited artifact.
docs/security/slither/*
!docs/security/slither/.gitkeep
!docs/security/slither/markets-dynamic-market.txt
!docs/security/slither/markets-dynamic-market.json

# Local Replit sync notes — never commit
REPLIT_SYNC.*
.vercel
.env*
# Re-negate after the catch-all above — the templates stay tracked.
!.env.example

# esbuild-bundled server for the Vercel function (generated at build)
api/_server.mjs
api/_dcw.mjs
api/_ubk.mjs
